To find the equation of the line in the form $y = mx + b$, we first express $x$ and $y$ in terms of the parameter $t$:
\begin{align*}
x &= 8 + 2t \\
y &= -1 + 3t
\end{align*}

Next, we can solve for $t$ in terms of $x$ from the first equation:
\begin{align*}
x &= 8 + 2t \\
x - 8 &= 2t \\
t &= \frac{x - 8}{2}
\end{align*}

Now, substitute this expression for $t$ into the equation for $y$:
\begin{align*}
y &= -1 + 3\left(\frac{x - 8}{2}\right) \\
y &= -1 + \frac{3x - 24}{2} \\
y &= \frac{-2}{2} + \frac{3x - 24}{2} \\
y &= \frac{3x - 26}{2} \\
y &= \frac{3}{2}x - 13
\end{align*}

The equation is now in the form $y = mx + b$, where the slope $m = \frac{3}{2}$ and the y-intercept $b = -13$.

\boxed{(\frac{3}{2}, -13)}

